From d7eed079ad13b59e1af3ad12285fcb2cfed528c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brunduk <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 05:23:35 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] t/constellation: trusted-orientation prior plumbed into the
 correspondence search (the deep fix for yaw ghosts)

The 0074 device-side gate rejects half-turn ghosts post-hoc, but by then
the search already PICKED the ghost (losing the true pose that frame) and
Camera::pushPose already poisoned last_known_pose. This closes the loop
at the source: a new optional get_trusted_orientation callback on
t_constellation_tracker_tracking_source lets the WMR controller supply
its fusion heading (Rx180-bridged into LED-model convention, gated on
solve_yaw_locked + WMR_CONSTELLATION_YAW_PRIOR_DEG, no new env). In the
tracker: pose_metrics_evaluate_pose_with_prior's reprojection-only else-if
branch (the code-located loophole) now also requires yaw-within-threshold
of the trusted prior; pose_metrics_score_is_better_pose prefers a
passing candidate over a failing one among already-good pairs; pushPose's
last_known_pose/blob-marking update is gated on trusted-yaw only for
opted-in calls (its unconditionality is documented load-bearing for
ordinary reacquisition -- byte-identical for every other device).
NULL-callback devices (rift, pssense, wmr_hmd) unaffected by construction.
Rate-limited tracker-side diagnostics distinguish this layer from 0074's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
